00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
roman abramovich said wednesday he is  selling his english soccer team chelsea  fc and will donate all net proceeds to  victims of russia's war in ukraine this  brings an end to his nearly 20-year  ownership of the club amid political  pressure for the british government to  sanction russian billionaires abramovic  said in a statement he's asked the team  to establish a charitable foundation  where he will donate all net proceeds of  the sale  for the benefit of all victims of the  war in ukraine the billionaire will not  ask for any loans to be repaid appearing  to allude to a 2 billion loan he lent  the club during his ownership his  announcement follows an attempt to  shield his ownership of the club by  handing control of it to the team's  charitable foundation over the weekend  which did not stop multiple members of  parliament from calling for sanctions  against abramovich  despite these calls for now prime  minister boris johnson has resisted  sanctioning oligarchs like abramovic as  of wednesday abramovic's net worth was  12.4 billion dollars down from 13.6  billion dollars on saturday abramovich  purchased chelsea fc for about 190  million dollars in 2003 and the team is  now valued at more than 3 billion  according to forbes estimates  [Music]
 

